<title>USA: U.S. cotton/weather summary - USDA/NOAA.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton/weather summary - USDA/NOAA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rainy weather associated with Hurricane Josephine slowed harvest activity in the Southeast and Gulf Coast states in the week of Sept. 30 to Oct. 6, a U.S. weather agency said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cool weather slowed defoliation of late-planted cotton fields in the southern Great Plains, the Joint Agricultural Weather Facility of the Agriculture and Commerce Departments said in its weekly report.</p>
<p>It said cotton condition continued to decline in Georgia due to high winds and heavy rains.</p>
</text>
